<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Merovech</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. mid-5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Merovech was a semi-legendary king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salian-franks">Salian Franks</a> in the mid-5th century, from whom the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merovingian-dynasty">Merovingian dynasty</a> took its name. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-of-tours">Gregory of Tours</a> says only that some held him to be of the family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodio">Chlodio</a> and that he was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/childeric-i">Childeric I</a>. A later legend in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-fredegar">Chronicle of Fredegar</a> gave him a sea creature as father.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/merovech.jpg" alt="Merovech" width="320" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bibliothèque nationale de France · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%A9daille_Roi_de_France_M%C3%A9rov%C3%A9e.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
